WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.090
Four hundred students, one

2
00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:05.350
assignment, two teaching assistants.

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:09.480
Last term the autograder passed code that

4
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.740
only worked on the visible tests.

5
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.540
How do you grade fairly at this scale?

6
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.320
Today: how to design autograded

7
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.080
programming assignments that measure

8
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.380
understanding, how to find and teach bugs,

9
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.840
and how to protect integrity when AI can

10
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:28.380
write the code.

11
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:32.110
An autograder runs each submission against

12
00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.390
a test suite and reports a score.

13
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.930
It is fast and consistent.

14
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.300
But it only measures what the tests check,

15
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.600
so test design is assessment design.

16
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.740
Give students visible tests

17
00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:47.780
for fast feedback.

18
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.600
Keep hidden tests for edge cases

19
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.500
such as empty input, duplicates

20
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.240
and very large values.

21
00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.600
Code that hard-codes the

22
00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.420
visible answers then fails.

23
00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.280
This median passes the visible test

24
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.460
but fails on even lengths.

25
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.560
It always picks the middle element.

26
00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.650
A hidden test finds it, and the

27
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.470
feedback message should name the

28
00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.090
case without giving the fix.

29
00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.970
Tests check correctness, not

30
00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:20.350
design or understanding.

31
00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:23.730
Combine an autograded part with a short

32
00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.770
code-reading task and a written

33
00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:26.230
explanation.

34
00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.900
Add a brief oral check

35
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.080
for a random sample.

36
00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.040
AI assistants can now solve most

37
00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.320
introductory assignments.

38
00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.650
Detection tools are unreliable,

39
00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:40.830
so design for it instead.

40
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.480
State clearly what help is allowed, weight

41
00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.980
in-person and explained work more, and ask

42
00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.480
students to modify or extend code live.

43
00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:53.120
Quick check!

44
00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.710
The median code passes the visible test.

45
00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:00.170
Which hidden test exposes its bug?

46
00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.780
A list with an even number of items,

47
00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:08.100
such as one, two, three, four.

48
00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.980
The correct median is two and a

49
00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.600
half, but the code returns three.

50
00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:16.970
In the app, open the bugs lab.

51
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.620
Find the failing case in each

52
00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.820
short program and write the hint

53
00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:22.700
you would give a student.

54
00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:24.780
Your turn.

55
00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.340
Which assessment change best shows that a

56
00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.720
student understands code they submitted?

57
00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.140
Asking them to modify it live

58
00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.400
and explain the change.

59
00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:38.890
Remember: hidden tests catch shortcuts,

60
00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:42.390
feedback names the case, and understanding

61
00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.270
needs more than a passing score.

62
00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.840
Try it in your next lecture: show a

63
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.600
submission that passes the visible

64
00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.200
tests and ask pairs to write one

65
00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.860
hidden test that breaks it.

66
00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.550
Collect the best tests and add

67
00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.010
them to next term's suite.
